/-!
# Chern classes and sections

Let `(S, δ)` be the base situation of chapter 42 of the Stacks Project, let `X` be a scheme
locally of finite type over `S`, let `ℰ` be a finite locally free `𝒪_X`-module, let `f : X' ⟶ X`
be locally of finite type and let `s ∈ Γ(X', f^*ℰ)`. The *zero scheme* `Z(s) ⊆ X'` is the closed
subscheme whose quasi-coherent sheaf of ideals is the image of `s : (f^*ℰ)^∨ ⟶ 𝒪_{X'}`.

[Stacks, Tag 0FA9] says: if `dim_δ(X') = n`, if `f^*ℰ` has constant rank `r`, if
`dim_δ(Z(s)) ≤ n - r`, and if for every generic point `ξ ∈ Z(s)` with `δ(ξ) = n - r` the ideal
of `Z(s)` in `𝒪_{X', ξ}` is generated by a regular sequence of length `r`, then

  `c_r(ℰ) ∩ [X']_n = [Z(s)]_{n - r}`  in  `CH_*(X')`.

This file holds the standing constructions of the section, the zero scheme `Z(s)` and the
regular-sequence hypothesis, and the reduction step of the source's proof for a bivariant class
characterized as in [Stacks, Tag 0B7H] against an abstract cap product rule. The lemma itself,
for the Chern class `c_r(ℰ)` of [Stacks, Tag 0ESW] and with exactly the source's hypotheses, is
`Stacks.Chow.SectionZeroScheme.chernClassOfLocallyFree_cap_fundamental_eq_zeroSchemeCycle`
(`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Chow.SectionZeroScheme.TopChernClassCap`) and
`Stacks.Chow.totalChernOfFiniteLocallyFree_cap_fundamentalCycle_eq_zeroSchemeCycle`
(`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Chow.ChernClassOfSection.TotalChern`).

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.Chow.zeroSchemeOfSection` — the zero scheme of a global section of a module of any
  rank, the construction of the standing situation of [Stacks, Tag 0FA8].
* `Stacks.Chow.IsRegularZeroSchemeSequence` — the regular-sequence hypothesis of
  [Stacks, Tag 0FA9]: at every generic point of `Z(s)` of `δ`-dimension `m`, the ideal cut out
  by `Z(s)` in the local ring is generated by a regular sequence of length `r`.
* `Stacks.Chow.TopChernCapEqZeroScheme` — the conclusion of [Stacks, Tag 0FA9] together with its
  hypotheses in the case `X = X'`, for an abstract cap product rule.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Chow.zeroSchemeOfSection_eq_zeroScheme` — for an invertible module the construction is
  the zero scheme of [Stacks, Tag 02OQ].
* `Stacks.Chow.cap_fundamentalCycle_eq_zeroSchemeCycle_of_isChernClassBivariant` — the
  reduction step of the source's proof of [Stacks, Tag 0FA9] (Stacks 0B7H): for a bivariant class
  characterized against a cap product rule, the equality on `X'` follows from the case `X = X'`
  for that rule.
* `Stacks.Chow.topChernCapEqZeroScheme_rank_one` — the case `X = X'`, `r = 1`, for a cap product
  rule identified with the first Chern class cap product, from [Stacks, Tag 02SQ].
* `Stacks.Chow.cap_fundamentalCycle_eq_zeroSchemeCycle_rank_one` — the two results above composed
  at rank one.

## Implementation notes

### Relation to the complete statement

The results of this file are stated for a `Stacks.Chow.HigherChernCapRule`, an arbitrary family
of cap operations, and a bivariant class characterized against it. The Chern classes of the
library are constructed (`Stacks.Chow.GenuineChern.chernClass`, assembled in arbitrary rank by
Stacks 0ESW), and [Stacks, Tag 0FA9] for them, in every rank `r` and with the source's
hypotheses, is proved by the source's induction over the projective space bundle in
`StacksDraft.AlgebraicGeometry.Chow.SectionZeroScheme` and
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Chow.ChernClassOfSection.Induction`; the registrations are the two
theorems named in the introduction above.

### The ideal cut out in a local ring

"The ideal of `Z(s)` in `𝒪_{X', ξ}`" is the kernel of the stalk map of the closed immersion
`Z(s) ⟶ X'` at the point of `Z(s)` over `ξ`, which is
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.stalkIdeal` of
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.MoreMorphisms.RelativeRegularImmersion.StalkIdeal` written out.
It is written out rather than imported so that this file depends only on the Chow directory.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0FA9](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FA9)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0FA8](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FA8)
